/*!
@defgroup linflexd_driver LINFlexD Driver (Linflexd)
@brief This section describes the programming interface of the Peripheral driver for LINFlexD.

# LINFlexD Driver Overview {#LINFLEXDDRIVEROvw}

The LINFlexD Controller is a semiconductor IP block supporting the Local Interconnect Network
(LIN) protocol for both master and slave applications.
The LINFlexD manages a high number of LIN messages efficiently with a minimum of CPU load. To
reduce the CPU loading in master mode, the LINFlexD autonomously handles the LIN messages
after software has triggered the header transmission, until the next header transmission request in
transmitter mode or until checksum reception in the receiver mode.
The LINFlexD supports LIN protocol versions 1.3, 2.0, 2.1, and 2.2, and provides an 8-byte buffer for
transmission/reception data.
The LINFlexD also supports a UART mode for UART transfers of 8-bit, 9-bit, or 13-bit data frames.
Optional DMA support is available for both transmit (Tx) and receive (Rx) data.<br />

*/